  "equipment_type": "Boiler burner management system (LMV52) via ProtoAir gateway",
  "applies_to": "Thermal Solutions and Bryan boilers fired by a Siemens LMV52 burner management system, connected to the Universal Gateway (ProtoAir FPA-W44).",
  "summary": "The ProtoAir Universal Gateway reads a Siemens LMV52 burner management system over Modbus and serves it on BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP. It reports the process value, flame signal, fuel flow, O2, combustion air and flue gas temperatures, efficiency, hours and the current lockout details, and lets the BMS set the control mode, operating mode, external setpoint, firing rate and process setpoint.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The table has no read/write column; AV and BV objects (N2 analog/digital outputs) are taken as writable.",
    "The manual gives no units, ranges or state texts for this profile; see the Siemens LMV5 documentation.",
    "AI 140-143 (lockout and diagnostic codes, fuel, firing rate) follow AI 27 with a gap in the numbering, as printed."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Universal Gateway Instruction Manual (ProtoAir): BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, N2, Modbus",
    "doc_number": "PN 106417-04 Rev A",
    "revision_date": "2024-05",
    "url": "https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/catsy.782/Universal+Gateway+ProtoAir+BACnet+Instruction+Manual.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Add the LMV52 as a profile in the ProtoAir Web Configurator with a unique Node-ID and discover it at 50000 + Node-ID. Read the process value, firing rate, flame signal and lockout codes; to run it from the BMS use the control mode, operating mode and external setpoint or fuel rate objects.",
